  "final_answer": "I have found the perfect course. Let me provide the final answer.\n\n## Answer\n\nI found a course on Coursera that matches your requirements:\n\n### **\"Introduction to Agile Project Management\"**\n- **Provider**: Chegg Skills\n- **Instructor**: Barry Finder\n- **URL**: https://www.coursera.org/learn/introduction-to-agile-project-management\n- **Part of**: Applied Agile Project Management Specialization\n\n### Course Details\n- **Level**: Beginner (初级) — Introductory level ✓\n- **Modules**: 1 module\n- **Recent Update**: August 2026\n- **Assignments**: 21\n\n### Why this course fits your requirements:\nThis is an **Introductory Project Management** course that extensively covers **Agile methodology**. The skills you will gain explicitly include:\n- ✅ **Agile Project Management**\n- ✅ **Agile Methodology**\n- ✅ Scrum (Software Development)\n- ✅ Cross-Functional Collaboration\n- ✅ Project Planning\n- ✅ Workflow Management\n- ✅ Backlogs\n- And more\n\n### What you'll learn:\n- Explain the principles of Agile project management and when Agile approaches are appropriate for managing projects\n- Describe the Agile Manifesto, Agile project lifecycle, and key artifacts used to organize and manage work\n- Identify the roles and responsibilities of Agile team members and how they collaborate throughout a project\n- Apply foundational Agile tools and practices to support project planning, collaboration, and delivery\n\nThis course is a direct match for an \"Introductory Project Management\" course with modules covering Agile methodology, with \"Agile Methodology\" being one of its core featured skills.",
